think Studied realidream_reader.rye (pin_read over editor.open_lane, read/ prefix guard) and mantra_editor.rye (commit continues a lane's head via head_revision + append_leaf; refuses LaneUnknown). A refresh is commit scoped to a read/ path.
think Authored pond/apps/realidream_reread.rye — refresh_read guards the read/ prefix (NotAReadPath) then delegates to editor.commit, so an unpinned read lane refuses LaneUnknown honestly. Three welcomes: grows the read lane r1 -> r2 with every program lane byte-identical; the earlier read still recalls its bytes (r1 first-read, r2 second-read) proving append-not-overwrite; refuses non-read and unpinned.
obs A re-read and a program edit are the same motion — an append the graph already knows how to show — so the read half inherits accrete-never-break by the same construction the editor did. No new abstraction; imports only public functions. Reads no network — refreshed content in-process; the real fetch stays the held seam.
